The calendar driver gives every "personal" calendar full rights. sabre/Baïkal reports a calendar
shared with the account as owned by the sharee, so a read-only share (MailHub's calendar subscriptions,
mailhub_dav + mailhub-mirror calsync) looked editable: edits were offered, then refused by the server.
A calendar whose share-access is read or read-write now takes the rights the server grants
(current-user-privilege-set). Worth proposing upstream (Kolab).

diff --git a/calendar/drivers/caldav/caldav_calendar.php b/calendar/drivers/caldav/caldav_calendar.php
index d84e351..a006b23 100644
